      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 145: `wantedState.applied` is set to `true` (line 135) *before* the request completes, but it is never reset when the request fails. In `onError` you only clear `pendingEndpointId`. As a result, if `requestCallEndpointChange` fails, a subsequent `endpointsChangedSubject` re-emission will short-circuit at `if (wantedState.applied) return@subscribe` and the target endpoint will never be retried — which partially defeats the resilience goal of this patch. Reset the flag on failure:\n```suggestion\n                                    override fun onError(error: CallEndpointException) {\n                                        if (pendingEndpointId \u003d\u003d endpointKey) pendingEndpointId \u003d null\n                                        wantedState.applied \u003d false\n                                        Log.e(TAG, \"setWantedAudioState endpoint failed: $endpoint\", error)\n                                    }\n```",
      "revId": "996da057232b530169121222d1177c892ff7ee1a",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
