      "message": "[info] Line 227: Emitting the synthetic `DEFAULT_AUDIO_STATE` publishes a fabricated EARPIECE state (with a supported-route mask of only EARPIECE|SPEAKER) onto `audioStateSubject`, which is exposed publicly via `audioState`. On API 34+ the legacy route branch isn\u0027t subscribed, so this value isn\u0027t consumed internally here — but any external subscriber of `audioState` could momentarily observe a misleading earpiece/route state that doesn\u0027t reflect the real active endpoint. Confirm no UI consumer of `audioState` derives display state from this synthetic emission on 34+; if it might, gate the synthetic emit so it only drives the endpoint re-evaluation rather than the public audio-state stream.",
